          "distinct": true,
          "id": "27b0af7fb3a881db5791a89427a2650c06fd8e39",
          "message": "[ci][mesh] Improve ATOMesh dashboard visualization (#1555)\n\n* [ci][mesh] limit ATOMesh benchmark and dashboard triggers\n\n* Update ATOMesh benchmark dashboard publishing\n\nRestrict benchmark execution to scheduled runs or explicit manual dispatch.\n\nPublish results through github-action-benchmark and improve ATOMesh dashboard merging, detail popovers, and point styling.\n\n* [ci][mesh] Align Kimi-K2.5-MXFP4 benchmark config and add launch diagnostics\n\n- Align Kimi-K2.5 server args to match local test config: gpu_memory_utilization\n  0.9, max_num_batched_tokens 32768, max_model_len 32768\n- Replace HSA_NO_SCRATCH_RECLAIM with AITER_QUICK_REDUCE_QUANTIZATION=INT4\n- Add decode cudagraph capture sizes (step 8) for 1p1d (up to 256) and 2p1d\n  (up to 1024), set decode_max_num_seqs accordingly\n- Update 2p1d concurrency to [256, 512, 768, 1024]\n- Add dump_launch_info helper to print environment variables and full command\n  before starting each prefill/decode/router process\n- Print docker.env contents before srun in pd_slurm_job.sh\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Configure ATOMesh pd rank mapping for Spur cluster\n\n* Support decode-single-node layout for Kimi 1P2D benchmarks\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jasen2201 <yajizhan@amd.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-10T18:35:18+08:00",
