          "distinct": true,
          "id": "724f08d51ca4909175c96485b5c1d9585f2d1e91",
          "message": "[Bugfix] DeepSeek-V4: fix sglang/vllm plugin SWA after paged-SWA migration (#1417/#1423) (#1573)\n\nPR #1423 (\"content-addressed paged SWA\") migrated the entire shared V4 SWA\npath -- the index kernels (write_v4_paged_{decode,prefill}_indices), swa_write,\nand the shared model _attn_core -- from a per-request ring to a paged layout\naddressed by swa_block_tables/block_size, and its own commit message deferred\n\"the sglang/vllm plugin-bridge SWA layout\" as a follow-up. That follow-up was\nnever done, so the plugins still called the kernels with the removed\nstate_slot_per_seq/cs kwargs and crashed at server startup:\n\n  TypeError: write_v4_paged_decode_indices() got an unexpected keyword\n  argument 'state_slot_per_seq'\n\nduring init_cuda_graph_state (build_atom_v4_decode_graph_metadata_from_sglang),\nfailing the \"Accuracy (DeepSeek-V4-Pro TP8)\" sglang CI job. Beyond the crash,\nthe plugins still WRITE SWA into a per-request ring (swa_kv, state_slot,\nswa_cache_size; no swa_block_tables / windowed pool), so a blind kwarg swap\nwould make the paged index reads disagree with the ring writes.\n\nFix (plugin-only, no shared engine/kernel change): keep the ring pool but speak\nthe new paged ABI via a degenerate ring-emulating SWA block table. Every logical\nblock of a request maps to the request's single ring slot\n(swa_block_tables[bid, :] = state_slot) and block_size is set to cs\n(= swa_cache_size); the paged offset then collapses to the exact ring offset:\n\n  swa_kv[swa_block_tables[bid, pos//bs]*bs + pos%bs] == swa_kv[slot*cs + pos%cs]\n\n- sglang/vllm bridges: bind swa_kv as the flat [pages, head_dim] view and set\n  attn.swa_block_size = cs; add _build_swa_ring_block_tables (broadcast fill,\n  CUDA-graph-capture-safe via a persistent buffer in the graph-buffer classes);\n  set md.swa_block_tables in every decode/prefill metadata builder; repoint the\n  six index call sites to the paged ABI (block_tables=md.swa_block_tables,\n  block_size=cs; prefill adds swa_block_tables). The vllm persistent decode path\n  keeps its unchanged ring kernel write_v4_decode_indices_fused (already emits\n  slot*cs+pos%cs, consistent with the degenerate-table write).\n- sglang draft-extend wrapper: swa_kv is now flat, so derive cache_size from\n  attn.swa_block_size and pass swa_block_tables/swa_block_size.\n\nThis keeps the plugins on ring semantics (memory-bounded, correct without radix\ncache); the paged content-addressed #1417 fix stays engine-only. Porting the\nplugins to a real windowed paged pool (to fix #1417 under prefix caching there)\nis a separate follow-up.\n\nValidation:\n- Kernel equivalence: the degenerate-table paged decode kernel produces\n  byte-identical SWA offsets to the pre-#1423 ring formula for spec=0 (cs=128)\n  and spec=3 (cs=131).\n- End-to-end: replicated the failing CI job locally (rocm/atom-dev:sglang-latest\n  + this ATOM, DeepSeek-V4-Pro TP8, --disable-radix-cache --page-size 256).\n  Server reaches \"Application startup complete\" (no crash at CUDA-graph capture);\n  gsm8k 5-shot = 0.9515 flexible + strict (CI threshold 0.94), matching the\n  engine's validated ~0.952.\n\nNot covered here (follow-up): MTP/spec (cs != 128) and the draft-extend graph\nare outside the failing CI (spec=0); the emulation math holds but each needs its\nown validation.\n\nSigned-off-by: yihonglie <hyi@amd.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
