          "id": "d13bfb0c2c50ee04e11b305761de8a09aa70348a",
          "message": "feat(loader): --load_dummy init modes + EP loader/hash-routing robustness (#1636)\n\n--load_dummy now takes an optional value {empty,zero,xavier} (bare flag =\nempty = legacy skip-load). zero zeroes all params; xavier does\nxavier_uniform_ for bf16 and a constant target magnitude for fp4/fp8 packed\nweights, keeping the forward finite. Threaded through arg_utils/config as\nOptional[str]; initialize_dummy_weights runs before\nprocess_weights_after_loading.\n\nFixes bundled in:\n- Batched loader EP under-fill: _stage_task maps to the local expert id\n  BEFORE creating a staging entry. Under expert parallelism a non-local\n  straggler could recreate an empty entry after the param already flushed,\n  miscounted as \"under-filled\" (broke Qwen3-235B FP8 EP load).\n- hash_topk_triton clamps the expert id read from tid2eid to [0, n_routed):\n  a garbage tid2eid (dummy weights or a corrupt checkpoint) otherwise yields\n  out-of-range expert ids and an OOB gather -> GPU memory fault.\n- direct_register_custom_op is idempotent (skips if the op already exists),\n  so re-importing atom.model_ops (e.g. after a sys.modules wipe in tests) no\n  longer double-registers and crashes.\n\nTest/infra:\n- tests/test_dummy_weight_init.py covers zero/xavier fills.\n- test_openai_server gated behind ATOM_RUN_SERVER_INTEGRATION=1 (+GPU) so a\n  bare `pytest tests/` no longer spawns a real server and hangs.\n- wait_server_ready.sh detects \"Memory access fault\"/\"HSA_STATUS_ERROR\".\n- run-atom-workload skill: background steps via run_in_background, not `&`.\n- test_arg_utils_spec.py: drop redundant argparse re-import (ruff F811).\n- docs updated for the new --load_dummy value form.",
