          "id": "6fd80f1638eaf43dd7eed32aeb1477d92b0777c5",
          "message": "perf: derive V4 decode compress/write plan caps from graph_bs (#1639)\n\nUnify how V4 DeepSeek compress/write plans are sliced for the decode\nCUDAGraph path. `make_compress_plans` now takes `graph_bs` + `max_q_len`\nand computes both caps internally as `graph_bs * per_seq_bound`\n(compress: ceil(qlen/ratio); write: min(qlen, K_pool)), sentinel-filling\n`[n_actual, cap)` — which is exactly the `[bs, graph_bs)` CUDAGraph\npadding region. The cap depends only on graph_bs/max_q_len (fixed at\ncapture), so capture and replay dispatch identically-shaped kernels.\n\nKey effects:\n- write plan gains the same slicing compress already had: the decode\n  write grid shrinks from the full buffer (HCA r=128: bs*128) to\n  graph_bs*min(qlen, K_pool) (~qlen for qlen<=K_pool), up to ~32x\n  smaller for the HCA ratio; the H2D copy and sentinel fill shrink with it.\n- compress cap moves from a max_bs-global value to a per-graph-tight\n  graph_bs*ceil(qlen/ratio), so small-batch decode graphs launch\n  smaller grids.\n- `decode_capacity_per_ratio` is kept as an explicit compress cap for\n  the extend-shaped verify graph (dynamic token-count buffers that can't\n  use the graph_bs formula); its write plan stays full-buffer. graph_bs\n  and decode_capacity_per_ratio are mutually exclusive.\n- Remove the now-dead `num_write` param from `update_compressor_states`\n  (grid uses write_plan.shape[0]).\n- Bridges: vllm/sglang decode paths pass graph_bs; eager paths keep the\n  tight manual re-slice; sglang decode compress buffer sized\n  s*ceil(qlen/ratio) to match vllm (was flat s, undersized for mtp_k>=4).\n\nValidated: tests/test_compress_plan.py (9, incl. CG invariance +\n[bs,graph_bs) padding sentinel); full unit suite 622 passed. E2e V4-Pro\nGSM8K base 0.9538 / MTP3 0.953 / TBO+DPA(decode CUDAGraph) 0.9447 (all\nwithin baseline band); 8k1k1024c TBO+DPA throughput 40785 tok/s\n(neutral vs ~41000 baseline).",
