          "id": "17dd229cd00acca44deaea410f2b0f51060ca53b",
          "message": "docs: editorial style pass across all docs (Google developer style guide) (#1650)\n\n* docs: apply editorial style pass to installation, quickstart, and architecture guide\n\n- Sentence-case all headings per Google developer style guide\n- Fix installation.rst: parallel subsection names, remove non-existent\n  env vars (ATOM_CACHE_DIR/ATOM_MAX_BATCH_SIZE), add AITER_LOG_LEVEL,\n  switch setup.py develop to pip install -e .\n- Fix quickstart.rst: correct API endpoint (/v1/completions), CUDA graph\n  casing, simplified batch loop, imperative heading style\n- Fix architecture_guide.md: promote Quick Reference from blockquote to\n  proper section, remove section numbers, add 'text' fences to ASCII\n  diagrams, replace -- with em dash throughout, remove hr separators\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndocs: restore load-balancing description in architecture guide\n\nAccidentally simplified step 3 of the request lifecycle and the source\nfiles table to say \"round-robin\" — restores the original wording that\ndescribes the configurable strategy (least_requests/round_robin/least_tokens).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: apply editorial style pass to all remaining docs\n\nAcross all 16 files:\n- Sentence-case headings (first word + proper nouns only)\n- Remove N. / N.M. section number prefixes from headings\n- Replace ' -- ' with ' — ' (em dash) in prose, not code blocks\n- Add 'text' language identifier to bare fenced blocks (ASCII art,\n  plain output, decision trees)\n- Remove decorative '---' horizontal rules between sections\n\nFiles touched: environment_variables.md, model_ops_guide.md,\ndistributed_guide.md, model_support_guide.md, configuration_guide.md,\nscheduling_kv_cache_guide.md, online_quantization_guide.md,\nserving_benchmarking_guide.md, hermes_agent_guide.md,\nmodel_run_guide.md, compilation_cudagraph_guide.md,\neagle3_speculative_decoding.md, vllm_plugin_backend_guide.md,\nindex.rst, api/models.rst, api/serving.rst\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: fix remaining Google style guide violations\n\n- Replace 'see below' with explicit anchor links in configuration_guide.md\n  and distributed_guide.md\n- Fix passive voice in model_support_guide.md ('is handled by' → active,\n  'is used by default' → 'ATOM uses ... by default')\n- Fix passive voice + future tense in scheduling_kv_cache_guide.md\n  ('is pushed / are deallocated / will be re-prefilled' → active present)\n- Fix second person in architecture_guide.md ('the user submits' → 'you submit')\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(installation): add MI350 to installation list\n\n* docs(installation, quickstart): reorganize with more descriptive text\n\n- Add intro paragraphs and section context to installation.rst\n- Add ROCm installation link with pre-install verification step\n- Explain Docker flags (--device, --ipc) and GPU_ARCHS values inline\n- Expand troubleshooting to three entries with concrete commands\n- Reorganize quickstart.rst into offline / distributed / API server sections\n- Add parameter explanations for gpu_memory_utilization, tensor_parallel_size\n- Expand performance tips with rationale for each recommendation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ncleanup\n\n* docs(installation): use amd-smi instead of rocm-smi\n\n* fix links\n\n* docs(api/serving): fix LLM→LLMEngine, return type, and SamplingParams note\n\n- Replace `from atom import LLM` and `LLM(...)` with `LLMEngine` — `LLM`\n  is not exported and would raise ImportError\n- Correct generate() return type from list[str] to list[dict]; show\n  outputs[i][\"text\"] access pattern throughout\n- Remove dtype parameter (not a Config field; silently ignored)\n- Fix SamplingParams note: top_p and top_k are supported; only\n  presence_penalty and frequency_penalty are not\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
