          "id": "f47f743ebc2ace7b6f9e56b3b5dab258c2c12742",
          "message": "fix: account for non-torch (RCCL) memory in KV cache sizing\n\nget_num_blocks sized the KV pool from PyTorch's allocated-bytes peak only,\nwhich excludes memory held outside the caching allocator: RCCL/NCCL channel\nbuffers and attention-backend scratch. On DP-attention + TBO this is ~14GB\nthat was never subtracted from the KV budget, so the pool was over-allocated\nand the runtime working set could exhaust device memory\n(HSA_STATUS_ERROR_OUT_OF_RESOURCES during an RCCL kernel launch).\n\nMeasure it as device-used minus torch-reserved (vLLM mem_utils.py style) and\nadd it to non_kv_overhead. Sizing-only change, no throughput impact\n(DeepSeek-V4-Pro DPA+TBO 8k/1k c=512: 31976 tok/s, unchanged); measured\nruntime alloc peak leaves ~46GB headroom with zero allocator retries.",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-20T16:46:16Z",
