          "id": "e3f9eb45c090dd18065bd4072ce3e176e98413a6",
          "message": "perf(tbo): compute prefill split scalars on host to cut D2H syncs (#1648)\n\n* perf(tbo): compute prefill split scalars on host to cut D2H syncs\n\nsplit_attn_metadata recomputed per-ubatch max_seqlen_q/k with per-field\n.item() calls, forcing one GPU->CPU sync each. Derive these from CPU\ncopies of the per-request length arrays instead:\n\n- attach_tbo_cpu_lens(): backends publish CPU (numpy) copies of\n  context_lens / cu_seqlens_q/k at the END of their own prepare_prefill\n  (opt-in, TBO-only, gated by tbo_enabled). _get_tbo_cpu_lens() reads\n  them (zero sync) and falls back to a one-shot lazy D2H if a backend\n  didn't attach.\n- max_seqlen_k / max_seqlen_q now computed from these host copies\n  (numerically identical to the device path, incl. straddling splits).\n- total_kv intentionally KEPT on the device path (ub_cu_seqlens_k):\n  backends override cu_seqlens_k for straddling token-midpoint splits,\n  so using the raw prepare-time copy would over-count KV and blow the\n  downstream index-kernel bounds.\n\nNon-TBO runs are unaffected (nothing attached, split path not reached).\n\n* fix(tbo): sync stream before restoring shared pinned buffers in V4 ubatch prefill\n\nThe host-scalar TBO path removed the per-ubatch .item() syncs that\nincidentally serialized async H2D copies reading from the shared pinned\nforward_vars buffers (context_lens/block_tables). In V4 ubatch prefill\nmetadata build, the finally-restore and the next ubatch then overwrote\nthose pinned sources before their copies landed, corrupting the paged-\nprefill index bounds the kernels consume (OOB / HSA_STATUS_ERROR_EXCEPTION\n0x1016).\n\nDrain the stream before the finally restore so the async copies land\nfirst. Scoped to the TBO ubatch prefill path; non-TBO is unaffected and\nthe host-scalar D2H savings are preserved.\n\n* style: reformat aiter_attention.py\n\n* perf(tbo): give V4 prefill ubatches their own metadata buffers\n\nRoot-cause fix replacing the finally+sync workaround. The prefill ubatch\nmetadata build borrowed the shared global forward_vars buffers\n(context_lens/block_tables), overwrote them, let helpers launch async H2D\nfrom them, then restored in finally. With the host-scalar path's .item()\nsyncs gone, that restore (or the next ubatch's borrow) could clobber the\npinned source before its non_blocking copy landed -> OOB index bounds\n(HSA 0x1016).\n\nInstead, each ubatch now reads/writes its own ub{idx}_ prefixed buffer\nset (context_lens / v4_batch_id_per_token / v4_n_committed_csa_per_seq /\nv4_indexer_cu_committed), mirroring the decode TBO path. No shared source,\nno restore, so no stream sync is needed -- overlap is fully preserved.\nThe ub{0,1}_ buffers are now allocated whenever enable_tbo is set (not\njust enable_tbo_decode).",
