          "message": "feat(cli): accept both --kebab-case and --snake_case for every flag (#1686)\n\nIntroduces FlexibleArgumentParser, a drop-in ArgumentParser whose\nadd_argument auto-registers the dash/underscore counterpart of every long\noption as an alias for the same dest. This generalizes the per-flag manual\naliasing added for --kv-cache-dtype in #1597 (now reverted to a single\nspelling) so ALL engine and entrypoint flags accept either form, without\neach add_argument spelling out both.\n\nOnly the flag name (after the leading --) is transformed, so option values\nare never touched — safe for JSON-valued flags like --online_quant_config.\nShort flags (-tp) and positionals are untouched; dest still derives from\nthe first option string, so existing callers are unaffected. An auto-alias\nthat would collide with an already-registered flag is skipped.\n\nRoutes the five parser creation sites (examples, openai api_server, atomesh\nserver) through FlexibleArgumentParser so entrypoint-specific flags benefit\ntoo, and points benchmark_serving's FlexibleArgumentParser alias at the\nreal implementation.",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T22:28:01+08:00",
          "tree_id": "3201a38f86d2d8797040ef3d9199db464b2def4c",
          "url": "https://github.com/ROCm/ATOM/commit/6a12488b4247dfc4c3a96cc18cd43f1d295b80c0"
