          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7b3d8db79ce76fabca89669715307b39a4f90de2",
          "message": "feat(benchmark): report Concurrency, Accept length and Acceptance rate (#1689)\n\nAdds three metrics to the serving benchmark output:\n- Concurrency: average in-flight requests = sum of per-request end-to-end\n  latencies / wall-clock duration (client-side, always printed).\n- Accept length: mean tokens per model forward (1 + accepted draft tokens).\n- Acceptance rate: fraction of drafted tokens accepted (accepted / drafted).\n\nThe two speculative-decoding metrics are fetched together from the server's\nexisting /debug/mtp_stats endpoint via get_spec_stats and printed only when\nspec-decode is enabled (get_spec_stats returns None otherwise, so the lines\nare skipped). All three are added to the result JSON, and the dashboard\ntracks Accept Length and Acceptance Rate (append_metric skips None, so only\nspec-decode variants emit those series). Docs output-metrics table updated.\nNo new dependency — aiohttp is already used by the benchmark client.\n\nVerified locally:\n- gpt-oss-120b tp1 1024/1024 conc64: prints Concurrency 62.36, correctly\n  omits the two spec lines (no spec-decode).\n- DeepSeek-V4-Pro MTP-3 tp8 1024/1024 conc64: Concurrency 57.29,\n  Accept length 2.21, Acceptance rate 40.17% (self-consistent).",
